WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.819
What happens to highly contaminated water
when it is placed in SCP-914, the Clockworks?

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:10.630
Dr. Ira selected one pint of highly contaminated
water for experimentation.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:14.910
It was placed into the machine on the setting
"Fine," and this was the resulting output:

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.890
A balloon-like instance resembling a Tardigrade.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.610
It was entirely translucent, and able to float
around the room.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:25.570
Dr. Ira then noted, “It wouldd appear that
all of the tissue making this thing up is

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:29.950
extremely loosely samples of bacteria in the
initial pint of water, in addition to small

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.250
water molecule chains holding it together.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.980
Apologies for the rule bending here, I'd honestly
completely forgotten about microscopic beings

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.770
in context of this thing.”

